{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4SNTpvQwVsxkuQKuss9Nn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/workspaces/launching-workspaces.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n1: # Launching Workspaces\n2: \n3: Use `launchWorkspace2` from `@openmrs/esm-framework` to open a workspace.\n4: \n5: ```tsx copy\n6: import { launchWorkspace2 } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n7: \n8: const MyComponent = ({ patientUuid }) => {\n9:   const openGastrodynamics = () => {\n10:     void launchWorkspace2('gastrodynamics-form-workspace', {\n11:       patientUuid,\n12:     });\n13:   };\n14: \n15:   return <button onClick={openGastrodynamics}>Open gastrodynamics</button>;\n16: };\n17: ```\n18: \n19: The full signature is:\n20: \n21: ```ts copy\n22: launchWorkspace2<WorkspaceProps, WindowProps, GroupProps>(\n23:   workspaceName,\n24:   workspaceProps,\n25:   windowProps,\n26:   groupProps,\n27: );\n28: ```\n29: \n30: - `workspaceProps` are passed to the workspace component as `workspaceProps`.\n31: - `windowProps` are shared by workspaces in the same window.\n32: - `groupProps` are shared by all windows and workspaces in the same group.\n33: - `null` or omitted props are considered compatible with existing props.\n34: \n35: `launchWorkspace2` returns a `Promise<boolean>`. It resolves to `true` when the workspace is launched or restored, and `false` when the user cancels a required close confirmation.\n36: \n37: ## Patient Workspaces That Require Visits\n38: \n39: For patient workspaces that require an active visit, use `useLaunchWorkspaceRequiringVisit` from `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib`.\n40: \n41: ```tsx copy\n42: import React from 'react';\n43: import { Button } from '@carbon/react';\n44: import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';\n45: import { useLaunchWorkspaceRequiringVisit } from '@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib';\n46: \n47: const OrderBasketActionButton = ({ patientUuid }) => {\n48:   const { t } = useTranslation();\n49:   const launchOrderBasket = useLaunchWorkspaceRequiringVisit(patientUuid, 'order-basket');\n50: \n51:   return <Button onClick={() => launchOrderBasket()}>{t('launchOrderBasket', 'Launch order basket')}</Button>;\n52: };\n53: \n54: export default OrderBasketActionButton;\n55: ```\n56: \n57: If visits are enabled and the patient has no active visit, O3 prompts the user to start or select a visit before launching the workspace.\n58: \n59: ## Behavior\n60: \n61: `launchWorkspace2` follows the workspace v2 group and window model:\n62: \n63: 1. If the target group is not open, O3 opens the group, opens the target window, and renders the requested workspace.\n64: 2. If another group is open, or if the existing group props are incompatible, O3 checks the affected workspaces for unsaved changes, prompts when needed, and then closes the current group and its windows.\n65: 3. If the target window is already open with compatible window props, launching an already-open workspace with compatible workspace props restores that window.\n66: 4. If the target window or workspace has incompatible props, O3 checks for unsaved changes before closing the window and opening a fresh instance.\n67: 5. `launchWorkspace2` does not create child workspaces. From inside a workspace, use the `launchChildWorkspace` prop supplied by `Workspace2DefinitionProps`.\n68: \n69: Workspace titles are set by the `<Workspace2 title=\"...\">` wrapper. The v1 `workspaceTitle` launch option is not used by workspace v2.\n70: \n\n(End of file - 70 lines total)\n</content>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b201a92-3f0b-4345-9c0c-2cc371256ed9","uuid":"4137d998-c8be-4d6d-a1a1-816a6122fc48","timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:02:48.105Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/workspaces/launching-workspaces.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<