{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCpn3VgeKtRTwQKXPbSn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The short answer: `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps, groupProps)` in the esm-styleguide package resolves the workspace's window and group from the registry, then compares the requested props with what is already open. If something incompatible is open, it asks the user to confirm before closing it. The docs describe the same behaviour.\n\n**Opening with props.** `workspaceProps` go to the workspace component, `windowProps` are shared by workspaces in the same window, and `groupProps` are shared by the whole group. A `null` or omitted prop counts as compatible with anything ([docs](openmrs-contrib-o3-docs/content/en-US/docs/workspaces/launching-workspaces.mdx) lines 19-35). The implementation throws if the workspace is unregistered, not attached to a window, or the window is not in a group. It then branches on the current state (`workspace2.ts` lines 133-321):\n\n1. **Different group, or incompatible group props.** It prompts with `CLOSE_WORKSPACE_GROUP`. On confirm it replaces `openedGroup` and sets `openedWindows` to just the new window and workspace. On cancel it returns `false`.\n2. **Window already open with compatible window props.** If the workspace is already in that window with compatible props, it restores the window when it is hidden or not the most recent, then returns `true`. Otherwise it appends the workspace to that window.\n3. **Window already open with incompatible window props.** It prompts with `CLOSE_WINDOW`, drops that window, and reopens it with only the new workspace.\n4. **Group is open and the window is not.** A `closable` group prompts with `CLOSE_OTHER_WINDOWS` and closes every other window. Otherwise the window is appended.\n\n**Conflict prompts.** `promptForClosingWorkspaces` (lines 398-430) collects the affected workspaces, and `showClosePrompt` (lines 363-382) shows a modal only if one of them has unsaved changes. A discrepancy to note: the doc comment at lines 392-394 says implicit closes prompt for all affected workspaces, but `getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow` (lines 348-361) only includes those with `hasUnsavedChanges`. I followed the code, which matches the launching docs' wording at line 64.\n\n**Group launches.** `launchWorkspaceGroup2` (lines 32-63) is a no-op if the same group with compatible props is open, otherwise it prompts and then replaces the group. `closeWorkspaceGroup2` (lines 74-96) closes the group and prompts only when windows are open.\n\n**Not checked:** the `Workspace2DefinitionProps` component file, the `launchChildWorkspace` path, and whether the other repositories call these functions beyond the one caller shown below.\n\nCitations use the `repo/path` form you asked for.\n\n**Implementation**\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `launchWorkspace2`, lines 133-321\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `launchWorkspaceGroup2`, lines 32-63\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `closeWorkspaceGroup2`, lines 74-96\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `promptForClosingWorkspaces`, lines 398-430\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `showClosePrompt`, lines 363-382\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow`, lines 348-361\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `arePropsCompatible`, lines 333-339\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts, `promptForClosingWorkspacesInWindow`, lines 439-444\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx